// Title: Driver Added To Disallowed Images In HVCI - Registry
// Sigma ID: 555155a2-03bf-4fe7-af74-d176b3fdbe16
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Omar Khaled (@beacon_exe)
// Date: 2023-12-05 | Modified: 2024-08-21
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects changes to the "HVCIDisallowedImages" registry value to potentially add a driver to the
//   list, in order to prevent it from loading.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of this key would also trigger this. Investigate the driver being added and make sure its intended
// References:
//   - https://github.com/yardenshafir/conference_talks/blob/3de1f5d7c02656c35117f067fbff0a219c304b09/OffensiveCon_2023_Your_Mitigations_are_My_Opportunities.pdf
//   - https://x.com/yarden_shafir/status/1822667605175324787
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_hvci_disallowed_images.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Control\\CI*" and RegistryKey contains "\\HVCIDisallowedImages"
